      "text": "Published: 16 June 2003 Skein-theoretical derivation of some formulas of Habiro Gregor Masbaum — We use skein theory to compute the coeﬃcients of certain power series considered by Habiro in his\n\n**Published: 16 June 2003 Skein-theoretical derivation of some formulas of Habiro Gregor Masbaum**\n\n20 pp, 7 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We use skein theory to compute the coeﬃcients of certain power series considered by Habiro in his theory of sl2 invariants of integral homol- ogy 3-spheres. Habiro originally derived these formulas using the qu antum group Uqsl2 . As an application, we give a formula for the colored Jones polynomial of twist knots, generalizing formulas of Habiro and Le for the trefoil and the ﬁgure eight knot.\n\n**Outline.** Introduction; 1 Habiro’s formula for ω; 2 A proof using orthogonal polynomials; 3 Graphical calculus and a formula for ω p; 4 Another formula for the coeﬃcients of ω p; 5 The colored Jones polynomial of twist knots; References\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Theorem 4.5: is equivalent to Habiro’s one from [H3]. (The res ults of Section 2\n- Theorem 3.2: The coeﬃcients cn,p of ω p in (23) are given by\n- Theorem 4.5: For p ≥ 1, the coeﬃcients c′\n- Theorem 5.1: The colored Jones polynomial of the twist knot Kp is given by\n- Proposition 2.1: The polynomials Sn satisfy a four-term recursion formula",
